select id, 'levels', '{"levels":[{"level":6,"marks":[26,30],"descriptor":"Convincing, critical and exploratory. A sustained, well-structured argument; quotations chosen precisely and woven in; perceptive analysis of the writer''s methods and their effects, with subject terminology used judiciously; context explored and linked convincingly to the writer''s ideas."},{"level":5,"marks":[21,25],"descriptor":"Thoughtful and developed. A considered, coherent response; well-chosen references; examination of the writer''s methods and effects with apt terminology; thoughtful links between context and the text."},{"level":4,"marks":[16,20],"descriptor":"Clear and explained. A clear response to task and text; effective use of references; clear explanation of the writer''s methods and their effects with relevant terminology; clear understanding of context linked to the text."},{"level":3,"marks":[11,15],"descriptor":"Some explanation. Some explained response; references used to support points; some identification and explanation of methods; some awareness of context."},{"level":2,"marks":[6,10],"descriptor":"Supported and relevant comments. Relevant comments backed by some reference; awareness of the writer making choices; some awareness of context."},{"level":1,"marks":[1,5],"descriptor":"Simple, explicit comments. Simple comments with little reference to the text; little awareness of methods or context."}],"indicative":["The list of verbs (''squeezing, wrenching, grasping...'') builds a picture of greed and isolation","Similes ''hard and sharp as flint'' and ''solitary as an oyster'' suggest he is closed off, though the oyster may hide a pearl, hinting at change","Cold imagery: he carries his ''own low temperature'', so his coldness separates him from others","He rejects Fred''s invitation and the charity collectors; people and even dogs avoid him","The Ghost of Christmas Past shows how he became isolated (lonely childhood, losing Belle)","By Stave 5 he is welcomed into family and society: the outsider is redeemed","Victorian context: the Poor Law and workhouses, Malthus (''decrease the surplus population''), Dickens''s concern for social responsibility","Dickens uses Scrooge''s isolation to criticise selfish attitudes to the poor"]}'::jsonb, '{"AO1":12,"AO2":12,"AO3":6}'::jsonb, 0 from q;

